LGPL dependency (binary redistribution only)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The `pxsmith` binary links `ansi_colours` (LGPL-3.0-or-later) through
`viuer` -> `pxsmith-view`. Rust links statically, so redistributing a built
`pxsmith` binary carries the LGPL-3.0 obligation to let recipients relink it
against a modified `ansi_colours` (LGPL section 4).

Distributing source, or the library crates on their own, does not:

  pxsmith-core / pxsmith-io / pxsmith-lint / pxsmith-recipe / pxsmith-macro / pxsmith-gen
                                                    -- no LGPL in the tree
  pxsmith-view / pxsmith (the binary)               -- LGPL via viuer

`icy_sixel` (no declared licence) is reachable only through the optional
`icy_sixel` / `sixel` features of `pxsmith-view`, which are off by default.
